    <statement><p>Consider the four functions graphed in the figure below, and assume the equations for <em>A, B, C,</em> and <em>D</em> can all be written in the form <m>y=ab^t</m>.</p>
<p>Which function has the largest value for <m>a</m>? <var form="popup">
<li>
<p>?</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>A</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>B</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>C</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>D</p>
</li>
</var></p>
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/sec-exp-functions-5-7-image-1.png" width="66%"/>
<p>(Click on graph to enlarge)</p>
</statement>
    <solution><alert>  SOLUTION </alert>



Since <m>y=a</m> when <m>t=0</m> in <m>y=ab^t</m>, <m>a</m> is the <m>y</m>-intercept.  Thus, the function with the greatest <m>y</m>-intercept, <m>A</m>, has the largest <m>a</m>.



</solution>
